  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">St. Kitts and Nevis Enhanced Public Sector Governance and Efficiency</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The recent economic crisis in 2009 has had a debilitating effect on the global economy and a new round of economic downturn threatens countries across the globe. St Kitts and Nevis (SKN) is no exception. The country&apos;s economy experienced contraction in 2009 and 2010, a slowdown in its tourism sector, pressures to its public debt and a decrease in tax revenue by 13.5% in 2010 . The country is on the path to recovery, but ensuring continued economic development and sustaining growth, would require tackling the country&apos;s public debt, particularly public expenditures, which includes an estimated public service wage bill of 14.96% for 2008/9.  For this reason, the country has implemented a public wage bill freeze and other measures to help improve efficiency of its public spending.  This IDF will help support the government implement these measures.</narrative>
  </description>
